From 24fa54bea3cb8de684271294bb2a28d185cb5f49 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: arealjim <6187715+arealjim@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:19:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] steam-frame client: video watchdog - reconnect when the
 receive thread stops reading, exit 4 when it is stuck

About 4 starts in 11 froze on the first frame (frame-lab C10, 2026-10-26): the server encoded and sent at
90 Hz, the client socket filled (Udp RcvbufErrors climbing) and no access unit completed again. The existing
reconnect rules never fire there: video did start, and a server that goes quiet is an idle app.

The new rule tells the two apart by the socket: FRAME_CLIENT_VIDEO_STALL_S seconds (default 2; 0 = off) with
no access unit AND datagrams unread in the video socket (FIONREAD) means the receive thread stopped reading.
The client then reconnects the way a lost stream does. Disconnect joins the receive thread, which may be the
stuck one, so a deadman exits with status 4 if Disconnect has not returned in 2.5 s (discovery's 1 s receive
timeout bounds a healthy one); a second stall within 15 s of a stall reconnect also exits 4, for a fresh
decoder. The frame-stream launcher restarts the unit on status 4 only.

